{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1523371345,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMTI5NTUwOTc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2405","origin":"github"},"title":"FOI: impact of changes in master on startup time of datalad commands","message":"#### What is the problem?\n x3-5 time slower for the same command(s):\n\n# install --help\n```shell\n\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/datalad; echo $dl; time $dl install --help | wc -l; done                                                                                           \ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n78\n$dl install --help  0.25s user 0.05s system 104% cpu 0.297 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.297 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n78\n$dl install --help  0.61s user 0.09s system 100% cpu 0.698 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.698 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n78\n$dl install --help  0.83s user 0.12s system 99% cpu 0.942 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.942 total\n```\n\ndifference washes out a bit while using a real command but still there and might be quite noticeable:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/datalad; echo $dl; rm -rf /tmp/123; time $dl install /// /tmp/123 1\u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 ; done\ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n$dl install /// /tmp/123 \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e\u00261  0.31s user 0.09s system 102% cpu 0.390 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n$dl install /// /tmp/123 \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e\u00261  0.50s user 0.12s system 94% cpu 0.651 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n$dl install /// /tmp/123 \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e\u00261  0.54s user 0.13s system 76% cpu 0.873 total\n```\n\nAnd for the mighty overall help:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/datalad; echo $dl; time $dl --help-np | wc -l; done                                                                                                \ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n167\n$dl --help-np  0.26s user 0.06s system 104% cpu 0.314 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.314 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n175\n$dl --help-np  0.72s user 0.11s system 100% cpu 0.825 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.825 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n180\n$dl --help-np  0.74s user 0.15s system 100% cpu 0.886 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.886 total\n```\nTo react to errorneous command - x1.5-2:\n```shell\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/datalad; echo $dl; time $dl bogus 2\u003e\u00261 | wc -l; done\ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n11\n$dl bogus 2\u003e\u00261  0.35s user 0.10s system 105% cpu 0.425 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.424 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n7\n$dl bogus 2\u003e\u00261  0.65s user 0.09s system 100% cpu 0.735 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.735 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/datalad\n7\n$dl bogus 2\u003e\u00261  0.63s user 0.09s system 100% cpu 0.718 total\nwc -l  0.00s user 0.00s system 0% cpu 0.718 total\n```\n\nFortunately impact on the special remote starter is not that sever (well -- up to 2x for -archives one somehow):\n\n```shell\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad; echo $dl; time time bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" 1\u003e/dev/null 2\u003e/dev/null; done\ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad\ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.38s user 0.18s system 95% cpu 0.583 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad\ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.62s user 0.16s system 100% cpu 0.774 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad\ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.54s user 0.12s system 100% cpu 0.656 total\n\n\n$\u003e for dld in datalad{,-master,-neuroimaging}; do dl=$dld/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad-archives; echo $dl; time time bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" 1\u003e/dev/null 2\u003e/dev/null; done\ndatalad/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad-archives                                                                                                                                           \ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.24s user 0.11s system 105% cpu 0.334 total\ndatalad-master/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad-archives\ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.51s user 0.11s system 101% cpu 0.615 total\ndatalad-neuroimaging/venvs/dev/bin/git-annex-remote-datalad-archives\ntime bash -c \"( cd /tmp/123; echo INITREMOTE | $PWD/$dl )\" \u003e /dev/null 2\u003e   0.44s user 0.12s system 101% cpu 0.549 total\n```\n\nFrom running\n```shell\n(git)smaug:~datalad/datalad-neuroimaging[master]\nDATALAD_LOG_LEVEL=2 DATALAD_LOG_TIMESTAMP=1 venvs/dev/bin/datalad --help 2\u003e\u00261 | ../datalad/tools/dtime 2\u003e\u00261 | less\n```\nI see major impact factors (number leading on the line is ms's until the next log line):\n```\n  268 2018-04-10 10:32:37,130 [Level 5] Importing cmdline.main \n    1 2018-04-10 10:32:37,398 [Level 5] Done importing cmdline.main\n  ...\n  122 2018-04-10 10:32:37,502 [DEBUG] Loading entrypoint neuroimaging from datalad.extensions \n    2 2018-04-10 10:32:37,624 [Level 5] Importing module datalad.distribution.create\n  ...\n  251 2018-04-10 10:34:16,543 [DEBUG] Building doc for \u003cclass 'datalad.support.sshrun.SSHRun'\u003e \n    5 2018-04-10 10:34:16,794 [DEBUG] Building doc for \u003cclass 'datalad_neuroimaging.bids2scidata.BIDS2Scidata'\u003e \n```\nIt is probably not the actual docbuilding for SSHRun but some import , since in 0.9.x:\n```\n    1 2018-04-10 10:36:32,929 [DEBUG] Building doc for \u003cclass 'datalad.support.sshrun.SSHRun'\u003e \n    2 2018-04-10 10:36:32,930 [Level 5] Importing module datalad.distribution.subdatasets  \n```\n\n.... more could be investigated to make it more sensible","files":null}]}